<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. rice major sales activity in the week ended Oct 24 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:	1996/97		 1997/98</p>
<p> Japan	    40,000		   Nil</p>
<p> Ivory Coast    11,500</p>
<p> Canada	   10,500</p>
<p> Germany	   2,600</p>
<p> Sweden	    1,900</p>
<p> Haiti	     1,700</p>
<p> Netherlands     1,100</p>
<p> Unknown	 -12,000</p>
<p>Net sales of 61,300 tonnes were 82 percent above the previous week and 17 percent over the four-week average.</p>
<p>Exports of 35,600 tonnes were one-third above the previous week but 26 percent under the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary export destinations: Ivory Coast (11,500), Nicaragua (9,000), El Salvador (4,500), Canada (2,700) and Mexico (2,400).</p>
</text>
